{"group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key", "literal": {"prompt": "Какое модное обозначение относится к одежде, выпускаемой партиями для массового рынка в стандартных размерах, а не для конкретного клиента?", "answers": ["От-кутюр", "Made-to-measure", "Bespoke", "Прет-а-порте"], "correctIndex": 3}, "ground": "The Met defines prêt-à-porter as multiples for the mass market in standard sizes and contrasts it with singular haute-couture models fitted to one person (L66). Merriam-Webster defines ready-to-wear as ready-made clothing, not for a particular person (L42-L46,L97-L99). The distractors are adjacent custom-production terms: made-to-measure is fashioned to specifically required measurements (MW L42-L44); bespoke is custom-made (MW L54-L62); haute couture is fitted to a specific individual (Met L66). Only option 3 matches standardized mass-market batches.", "locator": "L40-L48 defines clothing as ready-made; L60-L66 records first known use in 1895; L97-L99 says made in a standard size and not for a particular person.; L40-L44: fashioned to measurements specifically required; L54-L60: first known use 1885.; L52-L62 defines bespoke/custom-made and gives a bespoke suit; L109-L117 records first known use in 1607.; L66-L71 contrasts individual haute couture with mass-market prêt-à-porter; L78-L82 covers haute-couture embellishment by paruriers; L94-L97 defines toiles and full/half prototypes.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19cf4/source-fashion84/ready-to-wear-capture.json", "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19cf4/source-fashion84/made-to-measure-capture.json", "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19c7d/source-fashion83/bespoke-mw-capture.json", "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19c7d/source-fashion81/met-manus-x-machina-capture.json"]}
{"group": "explanation", "literal": "Прет-а-порте выпускают партиями для массового рынка в стандартных размерах. Merriam-Webster определяет ready-to-wear как готовую одежду, а The Met противопоставляет её единичным моделям haute couture, подогнанным по фигуре конкретного человека.", "ground": "The Met supports the prêt-à-porter mass-market/standard-size distinction and contrast with individually fitted haute couture (L66); MW defines ready-to-wear as ready-made (L42-L46).", "locator": "L40-L48 defines clothing as ready-made; L60-L66 records first known use in 1895; L97-L99 says made in a standard size and not for a particular person.; L66-L71 contrasts individual haute couture with mass-market prêt-à-porter; L78-L82 covers haute-couture embellishment by paruriers; L94-L97 defines toiles and full/half prototypes.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19cf4/source-fashion84/ready-to-wear-capture.json", "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19c7d/source-fashion81/met-manus-x-machina-capture.json"]}
{"group": "note0", "literal": "The Met пишет, что вышивку, перьевые украшения и искусственные цветы для haute couture создают мастера paruriers.", "ground": "The Met says elaborate haute-couture embroidery, featherwork and artificial flowers are made by paruriers (adornment makers), whose practices have changed little for over a century (L78-L82).", "locator": "L66-L71 contrasts individual haute couture with mass-market prêt-à-porter; L78-L82 covers haute-couture embellishment by paruriers; L94-L97 defines toiles and full/half prototypes.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19c7d/source-fashion81/met-manus-x-machina-capture.json"]}
{"group": "note1", "literal": "Merriam-Webster указывает, что первое известное употребление made-to-measure датируется 1885 годом.", "ground": "Merriam-Webster gives the first known use of made-to-measure as 1885 (L54-L60).", "locator": "L40-L44: fashioned to measurements specifically required; L54-L60: first known use 1885.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19cf4/source-fashion84/made-to-measure-capture.json"]}
{"group": "note2", "literal": "Merriam-Webster датирует первое известное употребление bespoke как прилагательного 1607 годом.", "ground": "Merriam-Webster gives 1607 as the first known use of bespoke as an adjective (L109-L117), distinct from the previously used bespoke etymology fact.", "locator": "L52-L62 defines bespoke/custom-made and gives a bespoke suit; L109-L117 records first known use in 1607.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19c7d/source-fashion83/bespoke-mw-capture.json"]}
{"group": "note3", "literal": "Merriam-Webster фиксирует первое известное употребление английского обозначения ready-to-wear в 1895 году.", "ground": "Merriam-Webster gives 1895 as the first known use of ready-to-wear (L60-L66); The Met identifies ready-to-wear/prêt-à-porter with mass-market standard-size garments (L66). The date is an extra fact about the correct option’s English equivalent.", "locator": "L40-L48 defines clothing as ready-made; L60-L66 records first known use in 1895; L97-L99 says made in a standard size and not for a particular person.; L66-L71 contrasts individual haute couture with mass-market prêt-à-porter; L78-L82 covers haute-couture embellishment by paruriers; L94-L97 defines toiles and full/half prototypes.", "sourcePaths": ["docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19cf4/source-fashion84/ready-to-wear-capture.json", "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a19c7d/source-fashion81/met-manus-x-machina-capture.json"]}
